Title: Interface sessions get a per-model context ceiling
Created: 2026-11-09
Author: reviewer

--- log ---
2026-11-09T22:05Z reviewer created

--- body ---
## Context

`rules/guards.md` stops every session at 230K tokens of context: past it the
task is too big and gets split. The author ruled on 2026-11-09, while
designing a relay pattern for long conversations, that interface sessions may
run longer: 450K on Sol or Opus, 550K on Astra or Fable.

The 230K number does three jobs. It bounds coherence, which depends on the
model. It signals a task too big to review, which does not. It bounds cost,
since every turn re-reads the context. An interface session converses with the
author and has no task to split, so only coherence and cost bind there; a
launched worker keeps the fixed number.

## Decisions

- **The exception is stated in `rules/guards.md`**, in one sentence, because
  no rule or skill overrides that file. An exception written only in the route
  skill would be void.
- **The numbers live in the route skill**, the single home for model facts.
  The rule names no model.
- **Any other model keeps 230K**, and so do launched workers, team leads and
  unattended runs. This is the executor's reading of a ruling that named four
  models; the author may widen it.
- **The compaction ban is untouched.** At its ceiling an interface session
  still stops and proposes a split. Whether a relay handoff may compact is the
  relay design's question, not this ticket's.

## Resident budget

The sentence adds 86 characters to the resident rules (15094 to 15180,
measured with `scripts/resident_census.py`). The cap had 6 characters of
headroom. Trimming 80 characters elsewhere would mean rewording guards the
author did not ask to change, so the cap rises by the same 86, to 15186. The
cost is about 31 tokens per session (derived: 86 / 2.8 chars per token, the
census's ratio, not measured).

## Exit criteria

- [x] `rules/guards.md` sends an interface session to its model's ceiling in
  the route skill, and names no model
- [x] `skills/route/SKILL.md` states the ceilings: Sol and Opus 450K, Astra and
  Fable 550K, any other model 230K
- [x] `RESIDENT_BUDGET` raised to the measured growth, with the reason in the
  test's comment; `STATE.md` restates the new cap
- [x] `make lint` and `make check-fast` pass
